6            User  ’s Guide to the Biosafety Act and Regulations

ABOUT THIS USER’S GUIDE


What is the purpose of this User    ’s Guide?


                 n 11 July 2007, Parliament passed the Malaysian Biosafet y
                 Act       2007.       The       Act       came       into       force       on       1       December       2009.
OThe                           Biosafet y                           (Aproval                           and                           Notification)                           Regulations
2010       were       passed       and       came       into       force       on       1       November       2010       to
implement                  the                  Act .                  Together                  they                  represent                  a                  new                  national
scheme      for      the      regulation      of      living      modified      organisms      (LMOs)1
and        products        of        LMO.        This        User’s        Guide        has        been        developed        as
a      resource      for      organisations      that       conduct      work      with      LMOs.      The
User’s        Guide        will        help        organisations        to        understand        and        comply
with the requirements of the new regulatory system for LMOs.

The    User’s    Guide    includes    chapters    on    each    of    the    key    aspects    of
the scheme including:

•                                                      Activities                involving                LMOs                that                are,                and                are                not ,                regulated
       under the national regulatory scheme;

•                                                      Regulation of import of LMO;

•                                                      Regulation of release activity involving LMO;

•                                                      Regulation of contained use of LMO;

•                                                      Regulation of export of LMO;

•                                                      Regulation of products of LMO;

•                                                      Confidential business information;

•                                                      Review of decisions made under the legislation;

•                                                      Reporting, monitoring and enforcement;

•                                                      The Malaysian Biosafety Website; and

•                                                      Fees and charges.


1                                            The term “LMO” refers also to genetically modified organism (GMO).

